tests/visual/output/
# Deliberately not committed. A golden here is held to an exact match, which is
# only possible because it never leaves the machine that wrote it: the driver
# deciding how alpha becomes a sample mask stays put, so the only thing that can
# move the bytes is the code. Committing them would mean loosening that to
# whatever the widest driver disagreement is, which is how a budget wide enough
# to pass a primitive that changed entirely gets set.
tests/visual/golden/
